for video segmentation with <math id="A2.T8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=80</annotation></semantics></math>, varying values of <math id="A2.T8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.T8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.T8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=16</annotation></semantics></math> and both binary and multiclass cases.
The maximum possible <math id="A2.T8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> for each case such that <math id="A2.T8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V&lt;32K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V&lt;32K</annotation></semantics></math> is highligted in yellow.
<math id="A2.T8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is shown in units of thousands.
</span></figcaption>
