for video segmentation with <math id="A2.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=128</annotation></semantics></math>, varying values of <math id="A2.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.T9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=16</annotation></semantics></math> and both binary and multiclass cases.
